  "title": "Temporal dynamics of short-term neural adaptation across human visual cortex",
  "status": "source_unresolved",
  "objective": "surpass_source_paper_same_task",
  "goal": "Surpass the source-paper result on the same task: Predict each selected visual electrode’s broadband response time course to single and repeated image presentations from stimulus timing and image category. The original performance comparator is the category-scaled DN model used in Figure 3C.",
  "primary_outputs": [
    "Candidate method and outputs for the source task: Predict each selected visual electrode’s broadband response time course to single and repeated image presentations from stimulus timing and image category. The original performance comparator is the category-scaled DN model used in Figure 3C.",
    "Source-paper comparison for Original Figure 3C region-wise cross-validated R² of the category-scaled DN model (scaling S): For each held-out trace, R² = 1 − sum_t(y_t−prediction_t)² / sum_t(y_t−mean(y))², using the pinned NaN handling; higher is better. Code rounds condition values to three decimals and fold means to four."
  ],
  "success_criteria": [
    "Recover full source cohort/input lineage and preserve all72 original conditions and visual areas. Use authenticated historical folds or a provenance-complete rerun of the exact original stochastic12-fold recipe after source-authorized protocol parity is established.",
    "Recover and calibrate Figure3C category-scaled DN using scalingS, original metric rounding and region aggregation. Predeclare a justified tolerance between the source published result and any stochastic author rerun; pair candidate and author on the same immutable fold realizations. Beating the weaker unscaled DN model alone is insufficient.",
    "Freeze candidate, meaningful effect, uncertainty and handling of all region summaries before final assessment. Preserve reported adaptation biology as supporting checks, not optimization targets.",
    "A changed splitting scheme, new participant holdout, reduced electrode set or alternate preprocessing is an extension. Missing historical RNG state alone does not make a faithful source-protocol rerun a different task; an arbitrary new fold recipe cannot substitute for source-protocol parity.",
    "The bound improvement contract must be improvement_ready and its complete same-task comparison and admission requirements must pass.",
    "Reproduction is calibration only; reconstructing a numerical result, changing the task or split, or achieving stronger significance alone is not success."
  ],
